Description: CVE-2026-84444 - validate tile images against the unci encoder configuration
 Out-of-bounds write in the uncompressed (unci) codec. heif_context_add_image_tile()
 passed independently constructed tile images straight to the uncompressed tile encoder
 (encode_image_tile()), which sizes its output buffer from the configuration frozen from
 the prototype image given to heif_context_add_unci_image() while copying from each tile's
 actual component planes. A tile whose colorspace, chroma subsampling, channel set, bit
 depths, tile size or plane sizes did not match that configuration wrote past the end of
 the encoder's output buffer (heap out-of-bounds write, CWE-787). A prior fix
 (CVE-2026-62291) validated component sizes only on the single-image encode() path, never
 on the tile-by-tile add path.
 .
 This is a hybrid backport of upstream commit
 e65071f59a1ac08aa1eb0d07a831deaf6bb4d03b (libheif v1.23.2, GHSA-j264-xvrp-5v7q).
 The upstream fix targets the stateful unc_encoder class introduced by a v1.22.0 refactor
 that does not exist in 1.19.8, so the guard is re-implemented against the older stateless
 tile path: ImageItem_uncompressed now freezes the prototype image configuration
 (colorspace, chroma, tile size, per-channel bit depths) in add_unci_item() and
 add_image_tile() validates every tile against that frozen configuration and its own plane
 sizes before encoding. An in-tree regression test adapted to the older test API is added.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/strukturag/libheif/commit/e65071f59a1ac08aa1eb0d07a831deaf6bb4d03b
Bug: https://github.com/strukturag/libheif/security/advisories/GHSA-j264-xvrp-5v7q
Author: Security Patch Automation <security@example.com>
